// SICA (Liu 2025, arXiv:2512.00665), instantaneous variant: unmix signals by
// iteratively descending the KL toward the DECOUPLED version of the current
// estimate. decouple(Z) is the dual of couple: the product of Z's empirical
// marginals -- same marginals, all dependence forgotten. Each round is one
// short KL descent (the samples-only nw field); Theorem 3.1 of the paper:
// the divergence is non-increasing over rounds. Watch the mutual information
// die: corr 0.94 -> ~0.02, histogram MI 1.09 -> 0.04 nats over 12 rounds.
seed 7

(X, S) = rv(mixed_sources(0.7)) ~ 1024  // one draw: observed mixture X + true sources S
Z = prob(X)                             // the demo works from X alone; S is kept for reference
plot Z                                  // heavily correlated (corr = 0.94)

for j in 1..12 {
    P = decouple(Z) ~ 1024          // product of current marginals: the round's target
    v = field(descent(reverseKL(P), from=Z), estimator=nw(kernel=rbf))
    Z = flow(v, steps=10, lr=0.5) # Z
    plot Z                          // per-round de-mixing, grouped by iter in the playground
}
